<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bijjala II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1168</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bijjala II was the most important ruler of the Kalachuris of Kalyani in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>. A feudatory and minister of the Western Chalukya king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tailapa-iii">Taila III</a>, he seized the capital Kalyani around 1156 and proclaimed himself emperor by 1162. His minister was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basava">Basava</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lingayatism">Lingayat</a> movement, and conflict with the movement marked the end of his reign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bijjala-ii.jpg" alt="Bijjala II" width="320" height="170" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kalachuris_of_Kalyana._temp_Bijjala.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
